```
  Detection : Account added to the local Administrators group
  MITRE     : T1098     Account Manipulation
              T1136.001 Create Account: Local Account
  Data      : Windows Security Event Log
              4720 = user account created
              4732 = member added to a security-enabled local group
  Why       : Attackers create or promote accounts to keep admin access
              even after the original malware is removed.
  Severity  : Medium (High if the account was created in the same hour)
  Author    : Ifeanyi Solomon Uneze
```
index=wineventlog (EventCode=4732 TargetUserName="Administrators") OR EventCode=4720
| eval action=case(EventCode=4720, "account_created", EventCode=4732, "added_to_admins")
| eval account_sid=coalesce(MemberSid, TargetSid)
| stats values(action) AS actions
        values(SubjectUserName) AS performed_by
        min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen
        BY host account_sid
| where mvcount(actions) > 0 AND isnotnull(mvfind(actions, "added_to_admins"))
| eval severity=if(mvcount(actions) = 2 AND (last_seen - first_seen) < 3600, "HIGH - created and promoted within 1h", "MEDIUM")
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)
| sort - severity

```
  TRIAGE
  1. Is there a change ticket for this admin grant?
  2. Who performed it (performed_by)? Is that account itself compromised?
  3. Has the new admin account logged on anywhere yet? (EventCode=4624)
```
